## Closure (2026-08-06)

Phased IDs **ED-VAL-01 … ED-LIST-CAT-01** met DoD (unit + live `denali.admin.localhost` where noted).

**v14 (2026-08-16):** Phase **11** / **ED-DT-RANGE-01** — inverted multi-day range was accepted at create Continue because `resolveDenaliDatetimeFieldMinIsoDate("endDateTime")` returned `undefined` and `mergeDenaliScheduleDateViolations` only emitted `DENALI_TOUR_START_BEFORE_TODAY`. Fix is Denali UI/validation only (no API, no `platform-core`).

**v15 (2026-08-16):** Phase **13** / **ED-PEAK-LOCK-01** — crafted POST/PATCH could store a peak/trail number other than the locked catalog value. Persist enrich runs on the HTTP/main thread inside `enrichValidateBeforePersistInput` (after optional catalog-ref allowlists, before worker/RuleEngine). `applyWorkspacePersistCanonicalNormalize` calls `wizardHost.normalizeCanonicalForPersist` only when the workspace implements it; otherwise it must not `listDestinations`. Denali `applyLockedDestinationCatalogMetricsToCanonical` overwrites `tripDetails.overview.peakHeight` / `trailDistanceKm` when the destination row locks that metric **and** the field is visible for the tour kind. Unlocked / missing destination / hidden field → leave operator values. API does not name `peakHeight` or branch on `plugin.id === "denali"`. Worker entry stays `validateCanonicalBeforePersistSync` on already-enriched `body.data`.

**v16 (2026-08-16):** Phase **14** — template/matrix hide already clears via `clearWhenNotVisible`. Visible-again did not re-seed catalog-locked metrics, so Continue validated empty canonical while the locked input painted catalog. Fix is Denali client persist + review/validation only: `seedEmptyVisibleDestinationCatalogMetrics` after sanitize (empty + visible + lock → catalog string; never a blanket `applyDestinationCatalogPrefill` on every keystroke). End clock: date picker must not re-commit the same local day. Numeric pairs: `min > max` only when both fields are visible and both set. Review: `participants.maximumAge` / `fitnessLevel` via `pushRowWhenFieldVisible`. `endDateTime` gains the same `clearWhenNotVisible` sibling as `approximateReturnTime`. No codegen unless generated rule rows change.

**v17 (2026-08-16):** Phase **15** — live create stored a populated gathering station in the composite then persisted `[]` because the field wrote `tripDetails.logistics.gatheringPoints` while `tourWizardDraftToDenaliForm` / review read root `gatheringPoints`. Promote nested→root in sanitize before form mapping; field/review use `resolveDenaliGatheringPointsFromStorage`. Catalog pickers: one soft-retry was not enough after cold BFF reset — degraded notice gains explicit retry + focus/visibility reload. File-input accessible name must not include the upload error string. No API / `platform-core` / `plugin.id === "denali"`.

**v18 (2026-08-16):** Phase **16** — remaining live-audit polish. Operator tour list/edit header used `Intl` currency style on hardcoded `priceCurrency: "IRR"` → «ریال» while wizard labels are تومان; same digits, no conversion. `formatTourPrice` special-cases `IRR` as تومان/toman. Nature destination + itinerary pickers omit peak catalog rows (`ED-DEST-NATURE-01`); selected peak stays listed so the control does not blank. `DENALI_TOUR_END_BEFORE_START` copy states the end must be **after** start (guard already rejects equality). Do not merge the two save buttons. No API / `platform-core` / `plugin.id === "denali"`.

**v19 (2026-08-16):** Phase **17** / **INV-DENALI-MULTI-CAL-A** — product picked invariant A: `*_multi` must span **at least two distinct local calendar days**. Old `estimateDenaliTourDayCount` clamped `days < 2` to `2`, so a same-day later clock still scaffolded two itinerary rows and photos treated `itinerary.length >= 2` as two days. Count is now inclusive local YMD from start/end (undefined when inverted/unparseable). Validation `DENALI_TOUR_MULTI_NEEDS_TWO_CALENDAR_DAYS` on `endDateTime` when the kind is multi and the span is 1. End date picker min for multi is start’s local day **+ 1**. Same-day later clock remains valid for single-day. No API / `platform-core` / `plugin.id === "denali"`.

**Operator follow-ups outside this pack** (not blockers; do not reopen lifecycle / platform-core validate):

| Item | Class | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Cold Next compile → intermittent BFF `503` on `/api/users`, `guide_languages`, drafts | Dev infra (mitigated) | Soft-fail notice + **one soft-retry** via `fetchDenaliCatalogJsonWithSoftRetry` on catalog pickers/destinations. Residual cold compile may still show degraded once. |
| Logistics / guide-language empty optional UX | Product polish | Empty state is valid when catalog soft-degraded or operator skips. |
| Day-photo hint / itinerary photo empty copy | Product polish | Non-blocking; out of edit-save critical path. |
| Unpublish `OPEN → DRAFT` | Non-goal | Lifecycle policy. |
| Portal CSS / auth gate on same git branch | Branch hygiene | Unrelated to this pack — split when committing. |

**Suggested exit:** Architect reviews this file; commit remediation + related web/api/denali diffs as one (or split API Doc-First) PR when ready. Prefer `pre-commit:fast` / listed verification — not full gates without YES.

**Debt audit (2026-08-06 v12):** Closed — Wave H list TZ twin in web i18n; firewall scope typo fixed; `resolveCanonicalRootsFromData` (no clone-only alias); invented-midnight named + one-shot end-field repair; catalog soft-retry helper; category warm failure + Retry (no infinite pending).

**ci:integrity contract sync (2026-08-06 v13):** Host specs lagged ED-DIFF / ED-UX soft-fail extraction — `DWC-STEP-06/07` still treated difficulty `"5"` as phantom (contradicts INV-DENALI-WIZ-010 + `DEN-RESUME-06b`); `WEB-DENALI-WIZARD-14` / `P15-W-C2` still required inline `i18n-errors` / `__error` on leaf fields after `DenaliCatalogLoadNotice` ownership. Updated those three web contracts only — no product logic change.

